.TH LOGGING-REVAMPED 1 "2026-11-17" "logging-revamped" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
logging-revamped \- capture a tmux pane to a file: live, scrollback or screen
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B logging-revamped
.RI [ options ]
.I command
.RI [ argument ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B logging-revamped
writes a tmux pane to a file in three ways: a live log that grows as output
arrives, the whole scrollback at once, or what the pane shows now. It also
follows, searches, copies, compresses and prunes those files. The entry point
.B logging-revamped.tmux
runs
.B apply
once when tmux loads the plugin, which binds the menu key and every action
key that is set, in one tmux call. Nothing runs until a key is pressed.
.PP
A file is named after the session, window and pane, a timestamp and its kind,
such as tmux-main-1-0-20260622-143005.history, with every character other
than a letter, a digit, a dot, an underscore or a dash written as a dash.
.PP
Run with no command on a terminal, it offers a menu.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B apply
Bind the keys and the status indicator now.
.TP
.B list
Print every tmux command apply would send, one per line, and change nothing.
.TP
.B toggle
Start or stop the live log of this pane.
.TP
.BI save " \fR[\fIlabel\fR]"
Save the whole scrollback to a file, with the label in its name when one is
given.
.TP
.BI screenshot " \fR[\fIlabel\fR]"
Save what the pane shows now.
.TP
.B label
Ask for a label in a tmux prompt, then save the scrollback under it.
.TP
.B window
Start a live log in every pane of this window.
.TP
.B clear
Clear the history of this pane.
.TP
.B tail
Follow the live log of this pane in a popup.
.TP
.BI search " \fR[\fIpattern\fR]"
Find a pattern in the plain logs, pick a match with fzf and open it at its
line in the pager. With no pattern it asks for one.
.TP
.B copy
Copy the newest plain log to a tmux buffer and the clipboard.
.TP
.B compress
gzip every plain log no pane is writing.
.TP
.B prune
Delete the logs past the retention settings, never one a pane is writing.
.TP
.B status
Print the indicator text for this pane.
.TP
.B doctor
Print one row per dependency: tmux, the log folder, gzip, fzf, the keys it
found bound, gum and the core tools.
A settings row names any setting whose value it does not know.
Exits 1 only when a required tool is
missing.
.TP
.B version
Print the version, then the tmux version.
.TP
.B help
Print the help page.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
.B list
prints one JSON object.
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " name"
Colours of the terminal interface:
.BR kodougu ,
.BR catppuccin\-mocha ,
.BR catppuccin\-latte ,
.BR dracula ,
.BR nord ,
.BR gruvbox ,
.B tokyo\-night
or
.BR mono .
The default is
.BR kodougu .
.TP
.BI \-\- setting " value"
Any tmux option below, named with dashes, such as
.B \-\-path
or
.BR \-\-retain\-days .
It also takes the form
.IR \-\-setting = value ,
and outranks the environment and the tmux option. Given to
.BR apply ,
it rides on every binding.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BI LOGGING_REVAMPED_ SETTING
Any tmux option below in capitals, such as
.BR LOGGING_REVAMPED_PATH .
It outranks the tmux option.
.TP
.B LOGGING_REVAMPED_THEME
The theme when
.B \-\-theme
is not given.
.TP
.B LOGGING_REVAMPED_ACCENT
A colour such as #CBA6F7 that replaces the accent of the theme.
.TP
.B KODOUGU_THEME
The theme of every kodougu and tmux-revamped tool, when neither
.B \-\-theme
nor
.B LOGGING_REVAMPED_THEME
is set.
.TP
.B KODOUGU_ACCENT
The accent of every kodougu and tmux-revamped tool, when
.B LOGGING_REVAMPED_ACCENT
is not set.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Turns colour off in every theme.
.SH TMUX OPTIONS
An empty tmux option means its default. A key set to off binds nothing.
.TP
.B @logging_revamped_menu_key
The prefix key that opens the logging menu. off binds nothing. The default is
M\-l, left alone when someone else holds it.
.TP
.B @logging_revamped_toggle_key
The prefix key that starts or stops a live log. The default is none.
.TP
.B @logging_revamped_save_key
The prefix key that saves the scrollback. The default is none.
.TP
.B @logging_revamped_screenshot_key
The prefix key that saves the screen. The default is none.
.TP
.B @logging_revamped_label_key
The prefix key that asks for a label and saves the scrollback. The default is
none.
.TP
.B @logging_revamped_window_key
The prefix key that starts a live log in every pane of the window. The default
is none.
.TP
.B @logging_revamped_clear_key
The prefix key that clears the pane history. The default is none.
.TP
.B @logging_revamped_tail_key
The prefix key that follows the live log in a popup. The default is none.
.TP
.B @logging_revamped_search_key
The prefix key that searches the logs. The default is none.
.TP
.B @logging_revamped_path
Folder of every file, made with mode 700 when first needed. A leading ~ is
expanded. The default is ~/.tmux/logs.
.TP
.B @logging_revamped_rolling
1 makes a live log append to one file per session. The default is 0.
.TP
.B @logging_revamped_color
1 keeps the colour sequences in a saved scrollback or screen. The default is
0.
.TP
.B @logging_revamped_output_only
1 drops the lines that match the prompt pattern from a saved scrollback or
screen. The default is 0.
.TP
.B @logging_revamped_prompt_pattern
An extended regular expression for the lines output\-only drops. The default
matches a line that starts with #, $, % or >.
.TP
.B @logging_revamped_pager
What opens a search match, run as pager +line \-\- file. The default is less.
.TP
.B @logging_revamped_retain_days
Above 0, prune deletes plain logs older than this many days. The default is 0.
.TP
.B @logging_revamped_retain_max
Above 0, prune keeps only this many of the newest logs. The default is 0.
.TP
.B @logging_revamped_status_on
What the status indicator shows while the pane is logged. The default is *.
.TP
.B @logging_revamped_status_off
What it shows otherwise. The default is nothing.
.TP
.B @revamped_theme
The theme of every tmux-revamped tool, when nothing else sets one. The default
is
.BR kodougu .
.PP
The placeholder #{logging_status} in status-left or status-right becomes a
format tmux draws itself. The plugin writes three options itself: the pane
option
.BR @logging_revamped_file ,
the file a logged pane writes to, and the global
.B @logging_revamped_prompt
and
.BR @logging_revamped_search_pattern ,
which carry a typed reply to the tool.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.tmux/logs
The default folder of the logs.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on any failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tmux (1),
.BR fzf (1),
.BR gzip (1),
.BR less (1),
.BR gum (1)
